course: dictionary
lesson: 11376
title: A magic word, and talk that makes no sense
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Abracadabra is a magic word. A magician waves a wand and says it before a trick, as if the word makes the magic happen. «The magician waved his wand and shouted, "Abracadabra!" and a rabbit appeared.» The words around it show that a magic trick is happening.
explain: Abracadabra has a second meaning too, and it is informal. If talk sounds clever or mysterious but you cannot follow it, you can call it abracadabra. «The instructions for the computer game were all abracadabra to me.» The sentence tells you the instructions made no sense to the speaker.
explain: Clues help you tell the two meanings apart. Ask yourself: is someone doing magic, or is something confusing? In a magic show, the word is part of a trick. When someone says «it's all abracadabra to me», they mean they don't understand.
fact: Abracadabra is a magic word that magicians say during a trick.
fact: «Abracadabra!» is often said with a wave of a wand, just before a rabbit comes out of a hat.
fact: Abracadabra is also an informal word for talk that sounds clever or mysterious but makes no sense.
fact: «It's all abracadabra to me» means I don't understand it at all.
fact: In ancient Rome, abracadabra was written on charms to protect people against illness, so it is a very old word.
exercise: The magician waved his wand and shouted, «Abracadabra!» What is the word used for? | A kind of rabbit | A word for a cold drink | *A magic word said during a trick | A name for a castle
exercise: «The maths homework was all abracadabra to me.» What does abracadabra mean here? | A long, quiet walk | *Words that made no sense to me | A magic trick that worked | A very kind teacher
exercise: Which word in this list is a magic word said by magicians? | hat | wand | *abracadabra | rabbit
test: «The new song lyrics were abracadabra to Sam, so he asked for help.» What does abracadabra mean here? | A magic spell that made Sam vanish | *Words that were hard to understand | A kind of animal | A happy song
test: In ancient Rome, people wrote abracadabra on charms. Why did they do this? | To make a rabbit appear | To name a new town | To tell the time | *To protect people against illness
exam: Which is the best explanation of abracadabra? | A kind of bird that sings at night | A type of cake eaten at parties | *A magic word, and also informal talk that makes no sense | The name of a Roman king
